  "_comment": [
    "Capability manifest for the evm-asm live-chain conformance harness.",
    "Single source of truth the harness reads to decide what it can run and to",
    "score opcode coverage against real blocks. Per-opcode `tier`, `witness`,",
    "and `cycles` mirror the kernel-checked registry surfaced in PROGRESS.md",
    "(EvmAsm/Progress.lean). Keep this file in sync with PROGRESS.md:",
    "`conformance/run.sh --check-manifest` diffs the two and fails on drift.",
    "",
    "`runtime` describes what the STANDALONE runtime_dispatcher guest does today:",
    "  exec  - executes with spec-faithful semantics (subset the demo runs live)",
    "  noop  - wired but fakes its effect (CALL/CREATE return 0; no real frame)",
    "  zero  - returns 0 / empty without real state (needs witness/preload)",
    "  absent- not in the EvmOpcode enum yet",
    "As evm-asm matures, flip `tier`/`runtime` here and the coverage % climbs",
    "automatically. See conformance/README.md for the stage roadmap."
  ],
